        <div class="g-team-roles g-team-roles--roster reveal">
          <article class="g-role-row">
            <h3>Doctors</h3>
            <p>MBBS and MD physicians, all credentialled by the CMO. Available on-site for clinic days and on WhatsApp
              for follow-up. Not teleconsultation operators — generalist doctors who learn your workforce.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="g-role-row">
            <h3>Care Managers</h3>
            <p>For elder care. Many are retired army personnel, nurses, or trained caregivers. They do home visits,
              manage hospital accompaniment, and handle the logistics of elderly care.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="g-role-row">
            <h3>Health Coaches</h3>
            <p>For post-clinic follow-through. They check in on employees with high-risk findings — elevated BP,
              pre-diabetic readings, high stress scores — and help them build a plan they'll actually stick to.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="g-role-row">
            <h3>Lab Coordinators</h3>
            <p>We coordinate between clinic, lab, and employee. Results come back to the employee's WhatsApp. No one is
              chasing a paper report two weeks later.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="g-role-row">
            <h3>HR Relationship Leads</h3>
            <p>Your single point of contact at Anara. They manage scheduling, employee communications, post-clinic
              reports, and any escalations. Your HR team should not need to manage us.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="g-role-row">
            <h3>Wellness Program Leads</h3>
            <p>For companies that want more than clinics: mental health programs, nutrition workshops, de-stress
              sessions. Led by qualified practitioners, not generic wellness vendors.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
