    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section id="faq" class="g-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
          <h2 id="faq-title">The six questions India HR Directors ask us first.</h2>
          <p class="section-sub">Direct and confident answers — not defensive ones.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="g-faq-list">
          <details class="g-glass-card g-faq-item">
            <summary><span>What participation rate can we realistically expect?</span><span class="chev"
                aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <div class="g-faq-body">
              <p>85%+ is our consistent range across client sites. We come during working hours, we come to your office,
                and we make it easy. The industry average for externally run programs is 40–50%.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="g-glass-card g-faq-item">
            <summary><span>Will this interfere with our existing TPA or broker arrangement?</span><span class="chev"
                aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <div class="g-faq-body">
              <p>No. Anara is preventive and primary care — not insurance. We sit alongside your GMC and TPA, not
                instead of them, and your broker relationship doesn't change.</p>
              <p>We've deployed at companies using HDFC Ergo, ICICI Lombard, Plum, Onsurity, and direct GMC contracts
                without any contractual conflict. On the first call we'll map exactly how Anara fits into your specific
                TPA + broker structure, and your broker can be part of the conversation if helpful.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="g-glass-card g-faq-item">
            <summary><span>How does Anara help avoid adding work and burden onto my HR team?</span><span class="chev"
                aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <div class="g-faq-body">
              <p>Your HR lead confirms the clinic date, shares the employee list, and sends the internal communications.
                Anara handles everything else — equipment, doctors, employee reminders, lab coordination, and the
                post-clinic report. Most of our HR contacts tell us we're the one health vendor they don't have to
                manage.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="g-glass-card g-faq-item">
            <summary><span>Can you cover our employees' parents as well?</span><span class="chev"
                aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <div class="g-faq-body">
              <p>Yes — this is one of our flagship programs. Anara's Care Managers do weekly home visits for enrolled
                parents across any of our service cities, plus on-demand telehealth. The Care Manager handles
                medications, lab coordination, hospital accompaniment, and sends real-time WhatsApp updates to the
                employee. It's the benefit that gets mentioned most in employee reviews.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="g-glass-card g-faq-item">
            <summary><span>What does executive health look like for senior leadership?</span><span class="chev"
                aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <div class="g-faq-body">
              <p>We send an Anara doctor to your office for a dedicated session with your senior leaders. More thorough
                than a standard health check: cardiovascular risk profiling, executive stress assessment, full blood
                panel, 1:1 consultation. No waiting. Full confidentiality. Leaders get a personal health summary and a
                12-month preventive plan.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <details class="g-glass-card g-faq-item">
            <summary><span>How does billing work?</span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <div class="g-faq-body">
              <p>Most clients structure payment through their OPD reimbursement budget or as a direct health services
                contract. We work on a per-employee per-year basis or per-engagement fee, depending on what makes most
                sense for your procurement structure. There's usually a clean path that doesn't require a new budget
                approval — we'll walk you through the options on the first call.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

